hebyshev-binomial-coefficient-estimate","ex-bertrand-finite-range-verification","ex-first-and-second-mertens-numerics","ex-third-mertens-product-numerics","cex-chebyshev-bounds-do-not-give-the-prime-number-theorem","cex-shoups-product-bound-does-not-determine-mertens-constant"],"conventions":[{"convention":"Elements of $L^p$ are almost-everywhere equivalence classes; pointwise arguments must choose measurable representatives.","fixed_by":"def-l-p-space-as-a-quotient-by-null-functions","matters_for":["thm-an-l-q-function-defines-a-bounded-linear-functional-on-l-p","prop-lambda-g-has-operator-norm-equal-to-the-l-q-norm","lem-l-p-functions-have-sigma-finite-essential-support-for-finite-p","cex-point-evaluation-at-zero-is-not-well-defined-on-l-p-of-unit-interval"]},{"convention":"For $1<p<\\infty$ the representation theorem is asserted for arbitrary measure spaces; at $p=1$, norm equality and uniqueness require the stated semifiniteness or sigma-finiteness hypothesis.","fixed_by":"prop-lambda-g-has-operator-norm-equal-to-the-l-q-norm","matters_for":["prop-semifinite-measures-make-l-q-representatives-unique","thm-sigma-finite-duality-for-bounded-functionals-on-l-p","thm-arbitrary-measure-duality-for-l-p-when-one-less-p-less-infinity","cor-l-p-norm-recovery-by-unit-l-q-pairings"]},{"convention":"The base normed-space convention is real, while the functional-analysis items allow the complex case by replacing real absolute value with complex modulus and retaining one common scalar field.","fixed_by":"rem-real-and-complex-normed-space-convention","matters_for":["def-bounded-linear-operator","def-bounded-bilinear-map","thm-bounded-linear-operator-equivalences","thm-bounded-bilinear-map-equivalences","ex-evaluation-functional-on-c-of-k"]},{"convention":"Quotient cosets are written $x+M$ and have seminorm $\\inf_{m\\in M}\\|x+m\\|=\\operatorname{dist}(x,M)$; no nearest point is assumed.","fixed_by":"def-quotient-seminorm","matters_for":["lem-quotient-seminorm-is-representative-independent","lem-quotient-seminorm-triangle-inequality","thm-quotient-seminorm-is-a-norm-iff-subspace-is-closed","thm-quotient-map-is-open","thm-quotient-of-banach-by-closed-subspace-is-banach","thm-universal-property-of-the-normed-quotient"]},{"convention":"The sequence-space examples and the counting-measure corollary index sequences from $n=0$.","fixed_by":"cor-ell-p-duality-by-counting-measure","matters_for":["ex-the-dual-of-ell-two-is-ell-two-by-the-counting-measure-pairing","ex-shift-operators-on-classical-sequence-spaces","cex-a-closed-subspace-need-not-have-a-best-approximation","cex-an-algebraic-complement-need-not-be-topological"]},{"convention":"The Chebyshev functions use real cutoffs, with $\\theta(x)=\\sum_{p\\le x}\\log p$ and $\\psi(x)=\\sum_{n\\le x}\\Lambda(n)$.","fixed_by":"def-chebyshev-psi-function","matters_for":["lem-chebyshev-psi-prime-power-expansion","lem-prime-counting-chebyshev-partial-summation","thm-chebyshev-theta-linear-bounds","lem-chebyshev-functions-prime-power-comparison","thm-chebyshev-prime-counting-bounds","ex-prime-counting-theta-and-psi-table"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-an-l-q-function-defines-a-bounded-linear-functional-on-l-p","statement":"For each $g\\in L^q(\\mu)$, $\\Lambda_g([f])=\\int fg\\,d\\mu$ defines a bounded linear functional on $L^p(\\mu)$ and $|\\Lambda_g([f])|\\le\\|[f]\\|_p\\|g\\|_q$.","used_by":["prop-lambda-g-has-operator-norm-equal-to-the-l-q-norm","prop-semifinite-measures-make-l-q-representatives-unique","lem-rn-densities-of-bounded-l-p-functionals-belong-to-l-q","thm-sigma-finite-duality-for-bounded-functionals-on-l-p"]},{"id":"prop-lambda-g-has-operator-norm-equal-to-the-l-q-norm","statement":"For $g\\in L^q(\\mu)$, $\\|\\Lambda_g\\|=\\|g\\|_q$ when $1<p<\\infty$, and also when $p=1$ provided $\\mu$ is semifinite.","used_by":["prop-semifinite-measures-make-l-q-representatives-unique","lem-rn-densities-of-bounded-l-p-functionals-belong-to-l-q","thm-sigma-finite-duality-for-bounded-functionals-on-l-p","thm-arbitrary-measure-duality-for-l-p-when-one-less-p-less-infinity","cor-l-p-norm-recovery-by-unit-l-q-pairings"]},{"id":"thm-sigma-finite-duality-for-bounded-functionals-on-l-p","statement":"On a sigma-finite measure space, every bounded $\\Lambda:L^p(\\mu)\\to\\mathbb R$ is integration against a unique $g\\in L^q(\\mu)$, with $\\|\\Lambda\\|=\\|g\\|_q$.","used_by":["thm-arbitrary-measure-duality-for-l-p-when-one-less-p-less-infinity","cor-ell-p-duality-by-counting-measure","rem-duality-as-a-dual-space-statement"]},{"id":"def-bounded-linear-operator","statement":"A linear $T:X\\to Y$ over one scalar field is bounded when $\\|Tx\\|\\le C\\|x\\|$ for all $x$ and some real $C\\ge0$.","used_by":["thm-bounded-linear-operator-equivalences","def-operator-norm","def-space-of-bounded-linear-operators","thm-bounded-operator-space-is-banach","thm-extension-of-a-bounded-map-from-a-dense-subspace","def-bounded-below-operator","def-bounded-left-and-right-inverses","functional-analysis examples"]},{"id":"def-quotient-seminorm","statement":"For $M\\le X$, $\\|x+M\\|_{X/M}=\\inf_{m\\in M}\\|x+m\\|=\\operatorname{dist}(x,M)$.","used_by":["lem-quotient-seminorm-is-representative-independent","lem-quotient-seminorm-triangle-inequality","thm-quotient-seminorm-is-a-norm-iff-subspace-is-closed","thm-quotient-map-is-open","thm-quotient-of-banach-by-closed-subspace-is-banach","thm-universal-property-of-the-normed-quotient","ex-c-mod-constants-and-oscillation-norm"]},{"id":"lem-central-binomial-coefficient-prime-valuation","statement":"$v_p\\binom{2n}{n}=\\sum_{k\\ge1}(\\lfloor2n/p^k\\rfloor-2\\lfloor n/p^k\\rfloor)$; in particular $v_p\\binom{2n}{n}=1$ for $n<p\\le2n$.","used_by":["thm-chebyshev-theta-linear-bounds","thm-bertrands-postulate","ex-chebyshev-binomial-coefficient-estimate"]},{"id":"thm-chebyshev-theta-linear-bounds","statement":"There are $0<c<C$ and $x_0$ such that $cx\\le\\theta(x)\\le Cx$ for every real $x\\ge x_0$.","used_by":["lem-chebyshev-functions-prime-power-comparison","thm-chebyshev-prime-counting-bounds","lem-weighted-von-mangoldt-harmonic-estimate","cex-chebyshev-bounds-do-not-give-the-prime-number-theorem"]},{"id":"thm-second-mertens-theorem-for-primes","statement":"$\\sum_{p\\le x}1/p=\\log\\log x+B_1+O(1/\\log x)$.","used_by":["thm-third-mertens-theorem-for-primes","cor-sum-of-reciprocals-of-primes-diverges","cex-shoups-product-bound-does-not-determine-mertens-constant"]},{"id":"thm-third-mertens-theorem-for-primes","statement":"$\\prod_{p\\le x}(1-1/p)=e^{-\\gamma}(1+O(1/\\log x))/\\log x$.","used_by":["cor-euler-prime-product-tends-to-zero","ex-third-mertens-product-numerics","cex-shoups-product-bound-does-not-determine-mertens-constant"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"cor-measurable-functions-admit-dominated-simple-approximations","used_for":"Simple approximants in the finite-measure Radon-Nikodym representation proof.","opened":true},{"id":"def-banach-space","used_for":"Completeness assertions for bounded-operator, extension, quotient, and bounded-below theorems.","opened":true},{"id":"def-binomial-coefficient","used_for":"Central-binomial definitions and estimates.","opened":true},{"id":"def-conjugate-exponents","used_for":"The $p,q$ exponent identities in $L^p$ duality.","opened":true},{"id":"def-countable-choice","used_for":"Explicit countable selections in measure and functional-analysis proofs.","opened":true},{"id":"def-dependent-choice","used_for":"Baire/open-mapping arguments and inverse criteria.","opened":true},{"id":"def-euler-mascheroni-constant","used_for":"The exact constant in Mertens' third theorem.","opened":true},{"id":"def-factorial-and-falling-factorial","used_for":"The factorial valuation formula.","opened":true},{"id":"def-finite-sigma-finite-and-semifinite-measures","used_for":"Finite, sigma-finite, and semifinite hypotheses in duality.","opened":true},{"id":"def-injection-surjection-bijection","used_for":"Topological isomorphism and closed-range criteria.","opened":true},{"id":"def-kern